  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nA cut off low pressure system will deepen over Oregon on \nWednesday, bringing a slight chance (15- 25%) of showers over \nsoutheast Oregon and high terrain in southwest Idaho. This low\npressure over the region will continue to bring unsettled \nconditions through early Saturday, with cool temperatures, \nperiods of light rain showers, and even a stray afternoon \nthunderstorm. The best chance of precipitation will be over \nhigher terrain in southwest Idaho and southeast Oregon. High \npressure looks to rebuild late Saturday, with a return to warm,\nslightly above normal temperatures, and dry conditions. Model \nsolutions diverge by Sunday, with hints at another trough \nbringing showers and slightly cooler temperatures. Other long \nrange models want to keep the ridge of high pressure over the \nWestern US through the early portion of the week.",
